<section class="claim-hero"><img src="/img/projects/roof-project-11.jpeg" alt="" aria-hidden="true"/><div class="claim-hero-shade"></div><div class="site-shell claim-hero-content"><p class="eyebrow eyebrow-light">Charlotte &amp; Rock Hill roof insurance documentation</p><h1>Roof Insurance Claim Documentation Support in Charlotte, NC</h1><p>Free roof inspections, factual storm-damage documentation, written roofing scopes, contractor supplements and adjuster-site coordination—from a fully insured, bilingual roofing team.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button button-gold" href="#claim-form">Request a free inspection →</a><a class="button button-ghost" href="tel:+19808005991">@Lang.T("Call Majestic")</a></div><small>Same-business-day response · 10-year workmanship warranty on qualifying replacements · English &amp; Spanish</small></div></section><section class="claim-proof"><div class="site-shell"><article><strong>5,000+</strong><span>roofing projects completed across claims, installations and repairs</span></article><article><strong>FREE</strong><span>inspection, photos, report and estimated measurements</span></article><article><strong>10 YEAR</strong><span>workmanship warranty on qualifying replacements</span></article><article><strong>EN / ES</strong><span>bilingual project communication</span></article></div></section><section class="claim-legal section"><div class="site-shell claim-legal-grid"><p class="eyebrow">Clear roles protect the homeowner</p><div><h2>A roofing contractor documents the work. Your insurance carrier decides coverage.</h2><p>Majestic Roofing inspects accessible roof areas, records visible conditions, prepares construction measurements and estimates, and explains its written roofing scope. With the homeowner’s authorization, the team may attend a scheduled adjuster visit and provide contractor scope clarification. Majestic Roofing is not a public adjuster, does not interpret policy language, does not negotiate coverage, and does not guarantee approval or payment.</p><a href="https://www.ncdoi.gov/consumers/disaster/after-storm/claims-and-adjuster-information" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">NC Department of Insurance claims resource ↗</a></div></div></section><section class="claim-process section" id="process"><div class="site-shell"><div class="section-heading split-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Five documented steps</p><h2>From storm concern to completed roof.</h2></div><p>Each step has a defined owner, record and decision point. The homeowner and carrier manage the insurance claim; Majestic manages the roofing evidence and construction scope.</p></div><div class="claim-step-list"><article><span>01</span><div><h3>Protect people and the property</h3><p>If a tree, open hole or active leak creates an immediate hazard, the first call may need to be 911, the utility, fire department or a qualified tree/structural professional. Majestic then confirms whether roof access is safe. When weather and conditions permit, temporary tarping may help limit additional water entry; the homeowner should preserve time-stamped photos, invoices and receipts.</p></div></article><article><span>02</span><div><h3>Inspect the roof as a complete system</h3><p>At the appointment, the technician first asks what happened, when it was noticed and which rooms are affected. The inspection can connect safe interior or attic evidence with the exterior roof area, then review accessible slopes, shingles, ridge and hip caps, valleys, flashing, pipe boots, vents, skylights, gutters, fascia, soffit and visible decking. Unsafe or inaccessible areas are clearly noted.</p></div></article><article><span>03</span><div><h3>Build a factual construction record</h3><p>Majestic organizes wide-location photos, detail photos, notes, estimated measurements, roof geometry, affected components, material observations and the proposed repair or replacement scope. Visible storm patterns are separated from age, maintenance, installation details and hidden conditions. The record explains physical roofing work without interpreting the insurance policy.</p></div></article><article><span>04</span><div><h3>Prepare for and coordinate the adjuster visit</h3><p>The homeowner reports the event, opens the claim and schedules the carrier’s adjuster. With homeowner authorization and a confirmed appointment, Eric or another Majestic representative may attend the property to identify the same documented roof locations, answer technical construction questions and explain the contractor estimate. The carrier independently evaluates cause, coverage and payment.</p></div></article><article><span>05</span><div><h3>Resolve construction scope, build and close out</h3><p>Majestic compares its roofing scope with the available carrier estimate. If documented quantities or necessary construction components differ, the company may submit a factual contractor supplement with measurements, photos and supporting construction details. After the homeowner approves the written agreement, Majestic schedules materials and installation, completes cleanup and provides final photos, invoice, applicable warranty and requested completion documents.</p></div></article></div></div></section><section class="claim-arrival section"><div class="site-shell"><div class="section-heading split-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">What happens at the property</p><h2>What the free inspection appointment includes.</h2></div><p>The goal is a clear, repeatable inspection—not a rushed photo from one roof spot. Safe access and property conditions determine which observations can be completed.</p></div><div class="claim-arrival-grid"><article><span>01</span><h3>Ten-minute roof interview</h3><p>We record the event, discovery time, weather conditions, active leaks, prior repairs and the rooms or exterior sides involved.</p></article><article><span>02</span><h3>Safety and access plan</h3><p>The technician identifies electrical, tree, structural, surface, slope and weather risks before choosing ground, ladder, roof, attic or drone viewpoints.</p></article><article><span>03</span><h3>Context before close-ups</h3><p>Overview photos establish each slope and roof feature. Detail images then document the exact location and visible condition without relying on isolated marks.</p></article><article><span>04</span><h3>Component-by-component review</h3><p>Shingles, caps, valleys, flashing, penetrations, ventilation, decking indicators and attached drainage components are reviewed as one system.</p></article><article><span>05</span><h3>Same-day explanation</h3><p>Majestic explains what was observed, what remains unknown, whether temporary work is recommended and the next repair, replacement or documentation step.</p></article><article><span>06</span><h3>Written handoff</h3><p>The homeowner receives available photos, report, estimated measurements and the written roofing path so the next decision is based on the same factual record.</p></article></div></div></section><section class="damage-section section" id="damage"><div class="site-shell"><div class="section-heading centered-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Observable roof conditions</p><h2>What storm damage can look like.</h2><p>These are educational inspection examples—not photographs of a specific Majestic customer and not promises that a policy covers the condition. Select any image for safety steps, a detailed arrival process and repair options.</p></div><div class="damage-grid"><a class="damage-card-link" href="/hail-damage-roof-inspection-charlotte-nc"><article><img src="/damage-guides/hail-damage-example.webp" alt="Educational example of hail roof damage" loading="lazy"/><div><b>01</b><h3>Hail</h3><p>Displaced granules, circular marks or fractures in shingle mats, damaged ridge or hip caps, plus dents in gutters, vents, pipe boots or other soft metals.</p><strong>Open detailed guide →</strong><small>Educational image · actual conditions vary</small></div></article></a><a class="damage-card-link" href="/wind-missing-shingles-repair-charlotte-nc"><article><img src="/damage-guides/wind-damage-example.webp" alt="Educational example of wind roof damage" loading="lazy"/><div><b>02</b><h3>Wind</h3><p>Missing, lifted, creased or displaced shingles; affected ridge caps, separated flashing and damage at soffit, fascia or roof edges.</p><strong>Open detailed guide →</strong><small>Educational image · actual conditions vary</small></div></article></a><a class="damage-card-link" href="/tree-roof-damage-charlotte-nc"><article><img src="/damage-guides/tree-impact-example.webp" alt="Educational example of trees &amp; debris roof damage" loading="lazy"/><div><b>03</b><h3>Trees &amp; debris</h3><p>Branch penetrations, broken or exposed decking, crushed shingles, damaged gutters and openings that may require safe temporary protection.</p><strong>Open detailed guide →</strong><small>Educational image · actual conditions vary</small></div></article></a><a class="damage-card-link" href="/active-roof-leak-repair-charlotte-nc"><article><img src="/damage-guides/active-leak-example.webp" alt="Educational example of active water entry roof damage" loading="lazy"/><div><b>04</b><h3>Active water entry</h3><p>Ceiling stains, attic moisture, wet decking and water paths that may begin upslope from the visible interior stain.</p><strong>Open detailed guide →</strong><small>Educational image · actual conditions vary</small></div></article></a><a class="damage-card-link" href="/chimney-flashing-leak-repair-charlotte-nc"><article><img src="/damage-guides/chimney-flashing-example.webp" alt="Educational example of chimney &amp; flashing roof damage" loading="lazy"/><div><b>05</b><h3>Chimney &amp; flashing</h3><p>Lifted metal, failed transitions, open counterflashing, deteriorated sealant or nearby shingle damage can allow water beside a chimney.</p><strong>Open detailed guide →</strong><small>Educational image · actual conditions vary</small></div></article></a><a class="damage-card-link" href="/open-roof-hole-decking-repair-charlotte-nc"><article><img src="/damage-guides/decking-damage-example.webp" alt="Educational example of open hole &amp; decking roof damage" loading="lazy"/><div><b>06</b><h3>Open hole &amp; decking</h3><p>Exposed, broken, soft or deteriorated plywood/OSB can require temporary protection, controlled removal and reconstruction by layers.</p><strong>Open detailed guide →</strong><small>Educational image · actual conditions vary</small></div></article></a></div></div></section><section class="credentials-section section"><div class="site-shell"><div class="section-heading split-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Publicly verifiable company signals</p><h2>Local roots with documented credentials.</h2></div><p>Majestic Roofing, Inc. was incorporated in North Carolina in 2021. Its technical team brings 25+ years of roofing-industry experience.</p></div><div class="credential-grid"><a href="https://www.bbb.org/us/nc/charlotte/profile/roofing-contractors/majestic-roofing-0473-92022094" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"><strong>A+</strong><span>BBB rating · 18 customer reviews · not BBB Accredited</span></a><a href="https://www.certainteed.com/profiles/majestic-roofing" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"><strong>2021</strong><span>CertainTeed ShingleMaster since 2021</span></a><article><strong>25+</strong><span>years of roofing-industry experience across the technical team</span></article></div></div></section><section class="scope-section section"><div class="site-shell scope-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">The contractor scope</p><h2>A roofing scope should explain the physical work—not the policy.</h2><p>Majestic organizes the construction facts so the homeowner, contractor and carrier can review the same roof components and quantities.</p><a class="button button-outline" href="/roof-insurance-supplements-charlotte-nc">Understand supplements →</a></div><ul><li>Roof measurements and geometry</li><li>Affected slopes and visible conditions</li><li>Shingles, ridge, starter and underlayment</li><li>Flashing, valleys and penetrations</li><li>Ventilation and related roof components</li><li>Gutters, fascia, soffit and soft metals when affected</li><li>Code or manufacturer requirements documented for construction</li><li>Labor, materials, disposal and written change conditions</li></ul></div></section><section class="carrier-section"><div class="site-shell"><p>CARRIER-NEUTRAL DOCUMENTATION EXPERIENCE</p><div><strong>STATE FARM</strong><strong>ALLSTATE</strong><strong>LIBERTY MUTUAL</strong><strong>AND OTHER CARRIERS</strong></div><small>Carrier names describe project experience only. No affiliation or endorsement is implied.</small></div></section><section class="eric-section section"><div class="site-shell eric-grid"><div class="eric-photo"><img src="/img/projects/roof-project-09.jpeg" alt="Completed Majestic Roofing shingle project"/></div><div><p class="eyebrow">Owner-led roofing</p><h2>Eric Benitez</h2><p>Eric grew up around roofing. His stepfather and family worked in the trade, and those early years taught him how roofing systems are built, inspected and repaired. Today, Eric participates personally in every Majestic project—from the first roof concern and documentation through scope review and construction coordination.</p><blockquote>Our job is to document the roof clearly, explain the construction scope and complete the work correctly. The carrier decides the policy.<cite>— Eric Benitez, Owner</cite></blockquote></div></div></section><section class="social-proof-section section"><div class="site-shell social-proof-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">Follow the work</p><h2>Project updates and customer education from Majestic.</h2><p>The official handle supplied by Majestic is linked here. Direct customer videos will be embedded after each exact post URL and website reuse permission are confirmed.</p></div><a href="https://www.instagram.com/majesticroofing1/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"><span>INSTAGRAM</span><strong>@@majesticroofing1</strong><b>Open profile ↗</b></a></div></section><section class="guide-links section"><div class="site-shell"><a href="/roof-adjuster-visit-guide-charlotte-nc"><span>01</span><div><p>BEFORE THE APPOINTMENT</p><h2>Prepare for the roof adjuster visit</h2></div><b>→</b></a><a href="/roof-insurance-supplements-charlotte-nc"><span>02</span><div><p>WHEN THE SCOPE DIFFERS</p><h2>Understand contractor supplements</h2></div><b>→</b></a><a href="/roof-warranty-transfer"><span>03</span><div><p>NEW PROPERTY OWNER</p><h2>Request a warranty transfer review</h2></div><b>→</b></a></div></section><section class="faq-section section" id="faq"><div class="site-shell faq-layout"><div><p class="eyebrow">@Lang.T("FAQ")</p><h2>Roof insurance questions, answered carefully.</h2></div><div class="faq-list"><details><summary>Is the roof inspection free?<span>+</span></summary><p>Yes. Majestic offers a free roof inspection for suspected storm damage, with no obligation. Availability depends on location, weather and safe access.</p></details><details><summary>Does Majestic file the insurance claim for me?<span>+</span></summary><p>No. The homeowner reports accurate facts and files the claim with the insurance carrier. Majestic can provide factual roof documentation, measurements and a written contractor estimate.</p></details><details><summary>What are ACV, RCV and depreciation?<span>+</span></summary><p>They are insurance-policy and payment terms. Their definitions and application depend on the specific policy and carrier. Ask the insurer or a licensed insurance professional for an interpretation. Majestic can provide roofing completion documents when requested.</p></details><details><summary>What is a roofing supplement?<span>+</span></summary><p>A contractor supplement is a factual request for review of construction scope, quantities, materials or documented conditions that may differ from the carrier estimate. It is not a guarantee of coverage or payment.</p></details><details><summary>Can Majestic meet the adjuster?<span>+</span></summary><p>When requested by the homeowner, scheduled and permitted, a Majestic representative may attend to point out documented conditions and explain the written contractor scope. The carrier independently evaluates the claim.</p></details><details><summary>Do you work with my insurance company?<span>+</span></summary><p>Majestic uses a carrier-neutral documentation process and has experience on roofing projects involving State Farm, Allstate, Liberty Mutual and other carriers. Majestic is not affiliated with or endorsed by any insurer.</p></details><details><summary>What warranty applies?<span>+</span></summary><p>Qualifying roof replacements include a 10-year Majestic workmanship warranty. Manufacturer warranty terms depend on the selected and documented roofing product.</p></details></div></div></section><section class="claim-form-section section" id="claim-form"><div class="site-shell claim-form-layout"><div><p class="eyebrow eyebrow-light">Start with documented facts</p><h2>Request your free roof inspection.</h2><p>Use this form for storm-damage inspection and claim-documentation requests. For an active emergency, call instead so the team can assess safe temporary protection.</p><a class="emergency-call" href="tel:+19808005991"><small>ACTIVE ROOF EMERGENCY</small><strong>(980) 800-5991</strong></a></div><form class="claim-form"><div class="claim-form-heading"><p>FREE ROOF INSPECTION</p><h2>Tell us what happened.</h2><span>Same-business-day response. No obligation.</span></div><div class="claim-form-grid"><label><span>Full name</span><input required="" autoComplete="name" name="name"/></label><label><span>@Lang.T("Phone")</span><input required="" type="tel" autoComplete="tel" name="phone"/></label><label><span>@Lang.T("Email")</span><input type="email" autoComplete="email" name="email"/></label><label><span>Preferred language</span><select name="language"><option selected="">English</option><option>Español</option></select></label><label class="wide"><span>@Lang.T("Property address")</span><input required="" autoComplete="street-address" placeholder="Street, city, state, ZIP" name="address"/></label><label><span>@Lang.T("What happened?")</span><select required="" name="event"><option value="" disabled="" selected="">Choose one</option><option value="hail">Hail / storm</option><option value="wind">@Lang.T("Wind / missing shingles")</option><option value="tree">@Lang.T("Tree or debris impact")</option><option value="leak">@Lang.T("Active roof leak")</option><option value="chimney">Chimney / flashing</option><option value="unknown">Not sure</option></select></label><label><span>When did you notice it?</span><input placeholder="Date or approximate date" name="noticed"/></label><label><span>Is water entering now?</span><select name="activeLeak"><option>Yes / Sí</option><option selected="">No</option><option>Not sure / No sé</option></select></label><label><span>Insurance carrier (optional)</span><input placeholder="State Farm, Allstate…" name="carrier"/></label><label><span>Claim number (optional)</span><input name="claimNumber"/></label><label><span>Adjuster visit scheduled?</span><input placeholder="Date/time or not yet" name="adjuster"/></label><label class="wide"><span>Anything else we should know?</span><textarea name="details" rows="4"></textarea></label></div><label class="claim-consent"><input required="" type="checkbox"/> <span>I confirm the information is accurate and authorize Majestic Roofing to contact me about this roofing request. This form does not file an insurance claim.</span></label><button class="button button-gold full-button" type="submit">Request my free inspection <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></button><p class="form-note">Submitting opens your email app with the completed request addressed to Majestic Roofing.</p></form></div></section>
